### TF -- the ticket (Bug, Medium, label b1375-2026-11-09; nb RD-798, RD-799, RD-800)
- `<TF-SUMMARY>` = The log-sink test files: the job-line time mask hides text beside the time, two masks pin nothing within a state, one locale turns 12 cells red, one cell title is stale
- `<TF-BLUF>` = Four weaknesses in the test files that landed with pull request 182 (RD-798, RD-799, RD-800): one Major and three Minors, all in test code; the independent test review read the product change itself as right (44 of 44 flagged lines wrapped, route answers unchanged). The Major: the mask on the job line of the business-hours report, __tests__/rd798-log-injection-chat-and-learning.test.js line {L_MASKB}, also hides text placed right before or right after the time, so a marker before the time, a marker after it, or the time replaced by 'Invalid Date' each leave the cell 'C-BODY-HOURS OUT 198 201' green. Relayed from the review's record, not re-run here. {BLOB_FACT}
- `<TF-REC>` = Recommendation (a proposal, not decided): one test-only change, red first, then an independent review. (1) Make the job-line mask match only a date-time shape; the reviewer's offline-checked form is the regular expression ^( {3}\u2022 )\d[\d/.,: -]*?\d(?:\s?[AaPp]\.?\s?[Mm]\.?)?( - \d+ sheets \() with the flags gm, and add a negative case to 'MASK-JOB-TIME' for each of the three plants (a marker before the time, a marker after it, 'Invalid Date' each compare different). Relayed: the reviewer checked offline, not as a test change, that this shape still hides the time printed under en-AU, en-US, de-DE, en-GB, fr-FR, ja-JP and hi-IN and turns all three plants red; that it passes the whole cell suite is not measured. (2) For route 190, freeze one value per pinned state (day and night separately) with the masks removed from those cells, or drop the two masks from the cells since the states are already pinned. (3) Set LC_ALL and LANG for the server child in the harness, or compare the answers with a locale-free canon. (4) Retitle the cell at line {L_T799} of __tests__/rd799-log-injection-auth-and-storage.test.js to what it asserts, for example 'the state lines print the first 8 characters of the state and the cookie, and MISSING for an absent cookie'.
- `<TF-DET1>` = Finding 1 (Major), relayed from 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-07_B1365_evidence/residue.md (Finding 1, heading at line {L_RF1}) and the table row at line {L_TB1} of 1_Project_Definition/Briefs/2026-11-07_B1365_STATUS.md: the mask is the second of four in clockMasked (line {L_CLOCKMASKED} of the test file) and its declared purpose is the local time of a job line (cell 'MASK-JOB-TIME', line {L_MJT}); its replaced part is \S[^\n]*?, which starts at the first non-space after the bullet and runs lazily to ' - N sheets ('. On the printed answer the masked span is exactly the time text, so text right before or right after it is swallowed. Plants, each in backend/server.js line {L_JOB} (the job-line template) or line {L_TS} (const timeStr = date.toLocaleString();), each run with the cells named C-BODY-HOURS: a marker before the time; a marker after the time; the time replaced by 'Invalid Date'. Received: all three green (5 of 5 cells). Controls in the same runs: a marker in the header, Weekdays, Found, user, Jobs and 'more users' lines, a sheets number plus 1, and a marker after 'sheets (' each turned 'C-BODY-HOURS OUT 198 201' red. Cells attached: 'C-BODY-HOURS OUT 198 201' (line {L_OUT198}; green under the three plants, red under the controls) and 'MASK-JOB-TIME' (line {L_MJT}; green; it tests the time only, not the text next to it).
- `<TF-DET2>` = Finding 2 (Minor), relayed from residue.md (Finding 2, heading at line {L_RF2}): the masks at lines {L_MASKC} and {L_MASKD} (route 190's off-hours paragraph and the digits of 'Critical Issues (N)') are applied to both pinned states, though the masked text is fixed inside each state (day: 'Critical Issues (7)' and no paragraph; night: 'Critical Issues (8)' and the paragraph), so 'C-BODY-HOURS IN 190' (line {L_IN190}) and 'C-BODY-HOURS OUT 190' (line {L_OUT190}) compare one masked value for both and pin nothing of route 190's off-hours judgement; only 'C-BODY-HOURS LIVE' reads the paragraph's presence and the log hour. Plants, each green in both 190 cells: the printed count changed to redFlags.length + 2 (backend/server.js line 10577), a marker in the paragraph's first line (line 20100), in its Impact line (line 20101) and in its Action line (line 20102), the off-hours count plus 1. Two plants on the hour logic (hour > 22 changed to hour > 2 at line 20091, and the child's environment without a time zone at a night state) turn only 'C-BODY-HOURS LIVE' red.
- `<TF-DET3>` = Finding 3 (Minor), relayed from residue.md (Finding 3, heading at line {L_RF3}): twelve keys of the cell at line {L_CBODY} (keys p and h 162, 191, 195, 196, 197 and 203) go red under LC_ALL and LANG de_DE.UTF-8 (118 of 119 tests) and are green under the hosted shape C.UTF-8 with TZ=UTC, under en_US.UTF-8 and under en_AU.UTF-8 (119 of 119 each); the hosted runner's real locale is not measured. Cause: the answers print numbers through toLocaleString() in the server child's locale, which the harness inherits from the developer's environment, so a developer on a non-English machine sees the cell red.
